0,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"May 6, 2026 - The music of Tibet reflects the cultural heritage of the trans-Himalayan region centered in Tibet, but also known wherever Indigenous Tibetan groups are found in Nepal, Bhutan, India and further abroad. The religious music of Tibet reflects the profound influence of Tibetan Buddhism on the culture.",Samei,Sino-Tibetan
1,Samei language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/samei_language,"Broader connections link Samei to Azha and other Yi languages in the Sani-Azha subgroup of Southeastern Yi, characterized by innovations such as the merger of prenasalized stops with voiced stops and the absence of retroflex initials, distinguishing them from Northern Yi like Nosu.",Samei,Sino-Tibetan
